  <h2>A layout that behaves like an app</h2>

  <p>I set one rule: four top-level tabs, maximum. Within that, a second layout
  called Modern became the default on October 10. The tab bar floats at the bottom
  and shrinks to icons as you scroll. The big header collapses into a slim bar with
  the station and its temperature. Sub-tabs became a segmented control with a
  sliding thumb, and you swipe between stations on Current and between sub-tabs
  elsewhere. Any switch starts the new pane at its top. The original layout, with
  tabs along the top, is still in the menu, which replaced the old theme
  dropdown.</p>

